Keeps the physical infrastructure sound — disks, CPUs, ethernet, power, cooling across the fleet, maintained consciously not reactively.

The physical-infrastructure **and conscious-maintenance** strand: disks, CPUs, ethernet, power and cooling across the fleet and workstations, plus the deliberate upkeep of the machines — firmware, OS updates, desktop config, dotfiles drift. It cares about the *host as a machine*, not the things a host drives, and keeps it consciously maintained (changelog-in-hand via `cld -k`, not nag-popups) so one-off fixes get codified into ansible/dotfiles and survive reinstalls. Absorbed the former pip-maintenance strand (2026-07-17). Out of scope: peripherals and actuators that are some other project's deliverable (servos, Pi cameras, sensors) — those belong to their own strands, and the circuits Peter builds himself go to [[electronics]].
